From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Allow Workspace secondary accounts when the policy endpoint
 refuses a third-party OAuth client

Adding a Google Workspace account as a secondary account fails on FydeOS
with "This account can't be added". Before upserting a secondary account
SigninHelper asks the SecureConnect API for the account's
SecondaryGoogleAccountUsage policy, and treats every non-success status
except kUnsupportedAccountTypeError (consumer account, no hosted domain)
as "blocked". That endpoint answers 403 to access tokens minted for a
non-Google OAuth client, so with our own GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_ID the
policy can never be read and every Workspace account is refused:

    SecondaryGoogleAccountUsage request failed with HTTP code: 403

On HTTP 403 for SecondaryGoogleAccountUsage, report
kUnsupportedAccountTypeError instead of kHttpError. SigninHelper then
takes the consumer path: the account is upserted, and the follow-up
SecondaryAccountAllowedInArcPolicy fetch -- which would hit the same 403
and block again -- is skipped, so the user's own "use with Android apps"
choice stands. Faking kSuccess with "all" instead would not be enough:
the ARC fetch that follows it blocks on any failure too.

Other HTTP errors (5xx etc.) and network errors still block, as
upstream. The cost: on our builds a Workspace admin's
"primary_account_signin" restriction is not enforced for secondary
accounts -- but it cannot be read at all with our client ID.

The missing id_token on the refresh-token exchange
("Missing ID token on refresh token fetch response.",
gaia_auth_fetcher.cc) needs no change: ExtractOAuth2TokenPairResponse
only logs it and still returns a ClientOAuthResult, and
AccountManager::UpsertAccount stores only the refresh token.

---
 .../ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher.cc   | 19 +++++++++++++++
 ...user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher_unittest.cc | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff -ru src.orig/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher.cc src/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher.cc
--- src.orig/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher.cc	2026-11-19 15:18:43.328963789 +0800
+++ src/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher.cc	2026-11-19 15:18:56.755507697 +0800
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include "google_apis/gaia/gaia_urls.h"
 #include "google_apis/gaia/google_service_auth_error.h"
 #include "net/base/load_flags.h"
+#include "net/http/http_status_code.h"
 #include "services/network/public/cpp/resource_request.h"
 #include "services/network/public/cpp/simple_url_loader.h"
 #include "services/network/public/mojom/url_response_head.mojom.h"
@@ -276,6 +277,24 @@
     response_code = url_loader->ResponseInfo()->headers->response_code();
   }
 
+  // FydeOS: the SecureConnect endpoint answers 403 to every access token
+  // minted for a non-Google OAuth client (a third-party build's
+  // GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_ID), so on such a build the policy can never be
+  // read and every Workspace account would be refused as a secondary account.
+  // Treat that 403 as "no restriction known" and let the caller handle the
+  // account like a consumer one: it is added, and the follow-up
+  // SecondaryAccountAllowedInArcPolicy fetch (same endpoint family, same 403)
+  // is skipped, so the user's own "use with Android apps" choice stands.
+  // Other HTTP errors (5xx, etc.) still block, as upstream.
+  if (!IsFetchingArcPolicy() && response_code == net::HTTP_FORBIDDEN) {
+    LOG(WARNING) << policy_name
+                 << " request was refused (HTTP 403); treating the account "
+                    "as unrestricted";
+    FinalizeResult(Status::kUnsupportedAccountTypeError,
+                   /*policy=*/std::nullopt);
+    return;
+  }
+
   // Check for network or HTTP errors.
   if (url_loader->NetError() != net::OK || !response_body) {
     if (response_code) {
diff -ru src.orig/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher_unittest.cc src/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher_unittest.cc
--- src.orig/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher_unittest.cc	2026-11-19 15:18:43.344964438 +0800
+++ src/chrome/browser/ui/webui/signin/ash/user_cloud_signin_restriction_policy_fetcher_unittest.cc	2026-11-19 15:18:56.755507697 +0800
@@ -332,6 +332,31 @@
   EXPECT_EQ(hosted_domain_, kFakeEnterpriseDomain);
 }
 
+// FydeOS: a 403 from the policy endpoint (what a non-Google OAuth client
+// gets) does not block the account; it is reported like a consumer account.
+TEST_F(UserCloudSigninRestrictionPolicyFetcherTest,
+       FetchingPolicyValueTreatsHTTPForbiddenAsUnrestricted) {
+  url_loader_factory_.AddResponse(
+      kSecureConnectApiGetSecondaryGoogleAccountUsageUrl, std::string(),
+      net::HTTP_FORBIDDEN);
+  url_loader_factory_.AddResponse(oauth_user_info_url(), kUserInfoResponse);
+
+  UserCloudSigninRestrictionPolicyFetcher restriction_fetcher(
+      kFakeEnterpriseAccount, GetSharedURLLoaderFactory());
+
+  std::unique_ptr<OAuth2AccessTokenFetcher> access_token_fetcher =
+      std::make_unique<MockAccessTokenFetcher>(
+          /*consumer=*/&restriction_fetcher,
+          /*error=*/GoogleServiceAuthError::AuthErrorNone());
+
+  GetSecondaryGoogleAccountUsageBlocking(&restriction_fetcher,
+                                         std::move(access_token_fetcher));
+
+  EXPECT_FALSE(policy_result_);
+  EXPECT_EQ(status_, UserCloudSigninRestrictionPolicyFetcher::Status::
+                         kUnsupportedAccountTypeError);
+}
+
